From: AdobeWine
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: fall back to /etc/machine-id for the system UUID.

Flatpak sandboxes have no /var/lib/dbus/machine-id, so the SMBIOS UUID and board
serial became placeholders and Adobe licensing saw the machine as a new device.

Test: wmic csproduct get uuid gives the same value in the sandbox and out of it; Lightroom no device limit page.
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
@@ -2239,7 +2239,9 @@
     int fd;
 
     memset( uuid, 0xff, sizeof(*uuid) );
-    if ((fd = open( "/var/lib/dbus/machine-id", O_RDONLY )) != -1)
+    /* a Flatpak sandbox only has /etc/machine-id; same value, so the machine stays the same one for licensing */
+    if ((fd = open( "/var/lib/dbus/machine-id", O_RDONLY )) != -1 ||
+        (fd = open( "/etc/machine-id", O_RDONLY )) != -1)
     {
         unsigned char buf[32], *p = buf;
         if (read( fd, buf, sizeof(buf) ) == sizeof(buf))
